{
  "_comment": [
    "Pre-repair snapshot of the two rows changed by",
    "2026-08-17_unpack_song_attachment_urls.sql. Captured from the live table on",
    "2026-08-17, immediately BEFORE that migration was run.",
    "",
    "Why this file exists: the migration also wrote a backup into the table",
    "songs_attachment_repair_backup, but that table read back as EMPTY from the",
    "app's anon connection afterwards - either it captured nothing, or RLS is on",
    "with no policy and is hiding the rows. Rather than leave the rollback",
    "depending on which, the snapshot is archived here in git where it is",
    "unambiguous and survives the backup table being dropped.",
    "",
    "Nothing was actually lost in the repair: every DISTINCT url present before",
    "is present after. The repair only split packed entries, dropped one",
    "duplicated Google Doc url and one duplicated YouTube url, and replaced stale",
    "metadata (a type:'GDOC' field that described a Drive *file* as a Google",
    "*Doc') with the shape the app's own parseFileUrl() generates.",
    "",
    "To restore, run the restore_sql below in the Supabase SQL Editor."
  ],
